xnu 0485: premap the sw_ctrl pin page the w10 probe maps

Measured 2026-11-26 (0484 boot): `wifistage 14` -- the worker completed the cold
link and identity, logged `W6 auto load start`, TCSR, the AMSS read, the SMMU
map, the PCI PM state and `W6 bus master command=0x6`, then stopped with no
`W6 reset start`. The next call is `wifi_w10_probe()`, whose first statement maps
the SW_CTRL page (GPIO 82) -- the only pin page the premap did not cover.

It is mapped with the other pins on the boot thread, before touch takes the
TLMM block, and the premap line now prints its address.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
index 3b3d290..72d05f1 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
@@ -2351,10 +2351,20 @@ void
 mondrian_wifi_premap_pins(void)
 {
 	(void)wifi_map_pins();
-	wifi_log("W4 premap pins wlan=0x%lx perst=0x%lx bt=0x%lx",
+	/*
+	 * wifi_w10_probe() maps the SW_CTRL page (GPIO 82) on its first
+	 * statement; taken from the worker it hangs, like every other late
+	 * map. Map it here with the rest (measured 2026-11-26: stage 14, no
+	 * `W10 pads` line).
+	 */
+	(void)wifi_map_once(&wifi_sw_ctrl_page,
+	    WIFI_TLMM_BASE + WIFI_TLMM_PAGE_SIZE * WIFI_GPIO_SW_CTRL,
+	    WIFI_TLMM_PAGE_SIZE);
+	wifi_log("W4 premap pins wlan=0x%lx perst=0x%lx bt=0x%lx sw=0x%lx",
 	    (unsigned long)wifi_wlan_en_page,
 	    (unsigned long)wifi_perst_page,
-	    (unsigned long)wifi_bt_en_page);
+	    (unsigned long)wifi_bt_en_page,
+	    (unsigned long)wifi_sw_ctrl_page);
 	mondrian_log_flush_now();
 }
 
